From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h713: leave the NSI node disabled

well0nez pointed out that this node cannot bind: sunxi-nsi (0011) matches
"allwinner,sun50i-h713-nsi" and "allwinner,sunxi-nsi", while the node says
"allwinner,sun50i-nsi". CONFIG_SUNXI_NSI is also off in our defconfig, so
nothing has ever probed it.

Do not fix the compatible string. The driver's probe is an unverified
decompilation: it writes a controller reset and enable into the live bus
QoS block at 0x02020000, programs a "MIPS shared memory" window, takes the
MBUS reset line and requests SPI 63. None of that has been checked against
stock behaviour, and the running display firmware depends on the bus
setup U-Boot leaves behind. Binding it would change a working system for
no measured benefit.

Mark the node disabled so the description no longer claims an active
device, and say why. Keep its contents as the record of what 0011 expects.
No runtime change: the node was never bound.

Reported-by: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/cstenger/allwinner-h713-mainline/issues/4#issuecomment-6924775553

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -1911,7 +1911,14 @@
 			status = "okay";
 		};
 
-		/* NSI Bus Priority Controller */
+		/*
+		 * NSI bus priority controller. Deliberately disabled: the
+		 * 0011 driver (CONFIG_SUNXI_NSI, off) matches neither this
+		 * compatible nor verified registers, and its probe resets the
+		 * live controller. U-Boot's bus setup is what the running
+		 * display firmware has been qualified against. Do not enable
+		 * without checking the probe against stock first.
+		 */
 		nsi: nsi@2020000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-nsi";
 			reg = <0x02020000 0x10000>;
@@ -1921,7 +1928,7 @@
 				 <&ccu CLK_DRAM>;
 			clock-names = "pll", "bus", "sdram";
 			resets = <&ccu RST_MBUS>;
-			status = "okay";
+			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
 		/*
